1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,032
Models are the basic building blocks of your business logic

2
00:00:04,032 --> 00:00:09,197
and also the basic building blocks of a DPT project

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:12,585
You can think about models as SQL definitions

4
00:00:12,585 --> 00:00:15,710
which then materialize as tables or views

5
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:20,556
but we will see that there are much more to them

6
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:23,563
Probably for now what you need to know about models

7
00:00:23,563 --> 00:00:27,548
is that they are stored as SQL files in the models folder

8
00:00:27,548 --> 00:00:31,162
and they are not only simple SQL SELECT statements

9
00:00:31,162 --> 00:00:33,638
but they come with some extra features

10
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:37,338
For example models can reference other models

11
00:00:37,338 --> 00:00:41,387
so DBT knows some semantic dependencies between those

12
00:00:41,387 --> 00:00:46,713
and also you can use different scripts and macros in your models

13
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:48,520
Now let's see how they work in action
